WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.848
In the year 313, Zu Ti led his army to the south bank of the Yangtze River, preparing to cross north and recover the lost land.

00:00:08.198 --> 00:00:12.182
The soldiers stood on the bank, gazing at the wide river.

00:00:12.532 --> 00:00:19.252
When the boat reached midstream, Zu Ti picked up an oar, struck the water hard, and made his vow.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:24.594
The river water slapped against the boat, spray flying everywhere.

00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:31.472
He said: 'If I cannot recover the Central Plains, I will never cross this river again!' Hearing this, the soldiers' blood boiled with passion.

00:00:31.822 --> 00:00:36.550
Everyone raised their arms and swore the oath loudly together with him.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.420
The great army landed on the north bank and advanced toward the lost land, unstoppable as splitting bamboo.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:48.602
Zu Ti recovered large stretches of land, and the common people rejoiced.

00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:53.344
Laughter returned to the fields, and the villages came back to life.

00:00:53.694 --> 00:01:01.182
People use 'striking the oar midstream' to describe the resolve of making a firm vow for one's ideals.

